module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.Away.AdjoinRoot
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.Finiteness
public import StacksFrontier.Homology.PseudoCoherent.FiniteFree
public import StacksFrontier.Homology.PseudoCoherent.Relative.Composition
public import StacksFrontier.Homology.PseudoCoherent.Relative.TowerModule

@[expose] public section

/-!
# Shrinking the base ring to a localization away from one element

Let `R` be a commutative ring, `s : R`, and `Rs` a localization of `R` away from `s`. For a
finite-type `Rs`-algebra `B`, an object of `D(B)` is pseudo-coherent relative to `Rs` exactly
when it is pseudo-coherent relative to `R`. So relative pseudo-coherence is insensitive to
replacing the base ring by a principal localization of it — in geometric terms, to shrinking the
affine open of the target to a standard open of itself.

## Main results

* `PseudoCoherence.isModuleRelativelyPseudoCoherent_localizationAway_base`: a localization of `R`
  away from one element of `R` is pseudo-coherent, as a module over itself, relative to `R`.
* `PseudoCoherence.relativelyPseudoCoherent_iff_baseLocalizationAway`: the resulting equivalence
  for an object of the derived category.
* `PseudoCoherence.moduleRelativelyPseudoCoherent_iff_baseLocalizationAway`: the same for a
  module.
* `PseudoCoherence.moduleRelativelyPseudoCoherentFrom_localizationAway`: tag 0679 read on the
  algebras themselves in degree zero, in one fixed degree `m`.

## Implementation notes

**Why this is a consequence of tag 067D and not of tag 0679.**
`PseudoCoherence.localization_preserves_relativePseudoCoherent` (tag 0679) turns relative
pseudo-coherence over `Rs` into relative pseudo-coherence over `R`, and that is the only
direction it gives. The converse — the one a locality argument on the target needs — is the
`.mpr` half here, and it comes from `PseudoCoherence.relativelyPseudoCoherent_iff_of_comp`
(tag 067D), which is an *equivalence* and needs only that the intermediate algebra `Rs` be
pseudo-coherent relative to `R`. So the whole content of this file is that one hypothesis of
tag 067D, discharged for a principal localization.

**The presentation used.** `Rs` is presented over `R` by the single variable inverting `s`:
`Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.Away.AdjoinRoot` identifies it with
`R[x]/(s·x - 1)`, whose kernel is principal, generated by a non-zerodivisor, so the quotient has
a two-term finite free resolution and is pseudo-coherent. Tag 065H
(`PseudoCoherence.isPseudoCoherentFrom_polynomialPresentation_independent`) is what lets this one
presentation stand for every presentation in `PseudoCoherence.IsRelativelyPseudoCoherentFrom`.

The presentation has to be by `MvPolynomial (Fin 1) R` rather than by `Polynomial R`, since that
is the shape the predicate quantifies over; `MvPolynomial.uniqueAlgEquiv` moves the kernel
generator and its regularity across, and because the transport happens *before* any
pseudo-coherence statement is made, no complex is ever moved along a ring isomorphism.

The private lemmas in the first section — a finite free module is pseudo-coherent, a short exact
sequence with pseudo-coherent outer terms has a pseudo-coherent cokernel, the regularity of
`s·x - 1`, and the comparison between a restricted degree-zero complex and the restricted module
— are verbatim copies of lemmas that already exist as `private` lemmas of
`StacksFrontier/Homology/PseudoCoherent/Relative/Localization.lean` (and, for the last, of
`Relative/Module.lean`). They are duplicated because `private` is file-scoped; if those files
ever expose them, these copies should be deleted.

**Not to be confused with `PseudoCoherence.isModuleRelativelyPseudoCoherent_localizationAway`**
in `Relative/Localization.lean`, which localizes the *source* algebra `A` away from an element of
`A` with the base `R` fixed. Here it is the base itself that is localized, and the suffix `_base`
marks that. The two are related: the sibling lemma applied with `A := R` and `a := s` gives the
result here, but only once `R` is known to be pseudo-coherent relative to itself, which is not an
available statement; the direct presentation below avoids needing it.

## References

* [The Stacks Project, Lemma 15.82.11 (067D)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/067D)
* [The Stacks Project, Lemma 15.82.8 (0679)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0679)
* [The Stacks Project, Lemma 15.82.3 (065H)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/065H)
* [The Stacks Project, Definition 15.82.4 (065I)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/065I)
-/

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open StacksDraft.PseudoCoherence

namespace PseudoCoherence

universe u

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

/-! ### Pseudo-coherence of a quotient by a principal ideal generated by a non-zerodivisor -/

/-- Regularity is reflected by an isomorphism of algebras. -/
private lemma isRegular_of_algEquiv {R : Type u} {A : Type u} {B : Type u}
    [CommRing R] [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra R A] [Algebra R B]
    (e : A ≃ₐ[R] B) {x : A} (h : IsRegular (e x)) : IsRegular x :=
  ⟨fun y z hyz => e.injective (h.left (by simpa only [map_mul] using congrArg e hyz)),
    fun y z hyz => e.injective (h.right (by simpa only [map_mul] using congrArg e hyz))⟩

/-! ### The comparison between a restricted degree-zero complex and the restricted module -/

/-- Pseudo-coherence transports along an isomorphism of objects of the derived category. -/
private lemma pseudoCoherentFrom_of_iso {S : Type u} [Ring S]
    {K L : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} S)} {m : ℤ}
    (hK : IsPseudoCoherentFrom K m) (e : K ≅ L) :
    IsPseudoCoherentFrom L m := by
  obtain ⟨E, hE, a, hiso, hepi⟩ := hK
  refine ⟨E, hE, a ≫ e.hom, fun i hi => ?_, ?_⟩
  · have := hiso i hi
    rw [Functor.map_comp]
    exact IsIso.comp_isIso
  · rw [Functor.map_comp]
    exact epi_comp _ _

/-- Restricting the degree-zero complex on `M` along `f : S → A` is the degree-zero complex on
the restriction of `M`, so the two pseudo-coherence statements agree. -/
private lemma restricted_single_pseudoCoherentFrom_iff
    {S : Type u} {A : Type u} [CommRing S] [CommRing A]
    (M : Type u) [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] (f : S →+* A) (m : ℤ) :
    IsPseudoCoherentFrom
        ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u} f).mapDerivedCategory.obj
          ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of A M))) m ↔
      @IsModulePseudoCoherentFrom S _ _ M _ (Module.compHom M f) m := by
  let : Module S M := Module.compHom M f
  let e := ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u} f).mapDerivedCategorySingleFunctor 0).app
    (ModuleCat.of A M)
  exact ⟨fun h => pseudoCoherentFrom_of_iso h e, fun h => pseudoCoherentFrom_of_iso h e.symm⟩

/-! ### A principal localization is pseudo-coherent relative to the ring it localizes -/

/-- **A localization away from one element is pseudo-coherent, as a module over itself, relative
to the ring it localizes.** This is the hypothesis that
`PseudoCoherence.relativelyPseudoCoherent_iff_of_comp` (tag 067D) needs in order to move the base
of relative pseudo-coherence between `R` and `Rs`.

The presentation `R[x] ↠ Rs` inverting `s` has kernel generated by the non-zerodivisor `s·x - 1`,
so `Rs` has a two-term finite free resolution over the polynomial ring; tag 065H says that one
presentation suffices. -/
public theorem isModuleRelativelyPseudoCoherent_localizationAway_base
    {R : Type u} {Rs : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing Rs] [Algebra R Rs]
    (s : R) [IsLocalization.Away s Rs] :
    letI : Algebra.FiniteType R Rs :=
      IsLocalization.finiteType_of_monoid_fg (Submonoid.powers s) Rs
    IsModuleRelativelyPseudoCoherent (R := R) (A := Rs) Rs := by
  let : Algebra.FiniteType R Rs :=
    IsLocalization.finiteType_of_monoid_fg (Submonoid.powers s) Rs
  intro m
  let p : Polynomial R := Polynomial.C s * Polynomial.X - 1
  let eA : AdjoinRoot p ≃ₐ[R] Rs :=
    (Localization.awayEquivAdjoin s).symm.trans
      (IsLocalization.algEquiv (Submonoid.powers s) (Localization.Away s) Rs)
  let eP : MvPolynomial (Fin 1) R ≃ₐ[R] Polynomial R := MvPolynomial.uniqueAlgEquiv R (Fin 1)
  let α : MvPolynomial (Fin 1) R →ₐ[R] Rs :=
    (eA.toAlgHom.comp (AdjoinRoot.mkₐ p)).comp eP.toAlgHom
  have hα : Function.Surjective α :=
    (eA.surjective.comp AdjoinRoot.mk_surjective).comp eP.surjective
  have hePr : eP (eP.symm p) = p := eP.apply_symm_apply p
  have hr : IsRegular (eP.symm p) := by
    refine isRegular_of_algEquiv eP ?_
    rw [hePr]
    exact isRegular_C_mul_X_sub_one s
  have hdvd : ∀ x : MvPolynomial (Fin 1) R, eP.symm p ∣ x ↔ p ∣ eP x := fun x => by
    rw [← map_dvd_iff eP, hePr]
  have hker : RingHom.ker (α : MvPolynomial (Fin 1) R →+* Rs) = Ideal.span {eP.symm p} := by
    ext x
    have hx : (α : MvPolynomial (Fin 1) R →+* Rs) x = eA (AdjoinRoot.mk p (eP x)) := rfl
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker, hx, Ideal.mem_span_singleton, hdvd x, ← AdjoinRoot.mk_eq_zero]
    exact map_eq_zero_iff eA eA.injective
  have hpc : IsModulePseudoCoherent (R := MvPolynomial (Fin 1) R)
      ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars (α : MvPolynomial (Fin 1) R →+* Rs)).obj
        (ModuleCat.of Rs Rs)) :=
    isModulePseudoCoherent_of_ker_eq_span _ hα _ hr hker
  exact (isPseudoCoherentFrom_polynomialPresentation_independent
    ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} Rs) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of Rs Rs)) m).1.mp
    ⟨1, α, hα, (restricted_single_pseudoCoherentFrom_iff Rs _ m).mpr
      ((pseudoCoherent_iff_all _).mp hpc m)⟩

/-- **Relative pseudo-coherence does not see a principal localization of the base.** For `Rs` a
localization of `R` away from one element and `B` a finite-type `Rs`-algebra, an object of `D(B)`
is `m`-pseudo-coherent relative to `Rs` exactly when it is `m`-pseudo-coherent relative to `R`,
and likewise for pseudo-coherence.

The left-to-right implication is tag 0679 with a trivial localization of the source; the content
is the converse. Both come from tag 067D together with
`PseudoCoherence.isModuleRelativelyPseudoCoherent_localizationAway_base`. -/
public theorem relativelyPseudoCoherent_iff_baseLocalizationAway
    {R : Type u} {Rs : Type u} {B : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing Rs] [CommRing B]
    [Algebra R Rs] (s : R) [IsLocalization.Away s Rs]
    [Algebra Rs B] [Algebra R B] [IsScalarTower R Rs B] [Algebra.FiniteType Rs B]
    (K : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} B)) (m : ℤ) :
    letI : Algebra.FiniteType R Rs :=
      IsLocalization.finiteType_of_monoid_fg (Submonoid.powers s) Rs
    letI : Algebra.FiniteType R B :=
      Algebra.FiniteType.trans (R := R) (S := Rs) (A := B) inferInstance inferInstance
    (IsRelativelyPseudoCoherentFrom (R := Rs) K m ↔
      IsRelativelyPseudoCoherentFrom (R := R) K m) ∧
    (IsRelativelyPseudoCoherent (R := Rs) K ↔ IsRelativelyPseudoCoherent (R := R) K) := by
  let : Algebra.FiniteType R Rs :=
    IsLocalization.finiteType_of_monoid_fg (Submonoid.powers s) Rs
  exact relativelyPseudoCoherent_iff_of_comp
    (isModuleRelativelyPseudoCoherent_localizationAway_base s) K m

/-! ### Tag 0679 for the algebras themselves in degree zero -/

/-- **Tag 0679 for the algebras themselves in degree zero.** Let `Rs` be a localization of `R`
away from `s : R`, let `A` be a finite-type `Rs`-algebra and let `Aa` be a localization of `A`
away from `a : A`. If `A` is `m`-pseudo-coherent relative to `Rs` as a module over itself, then
`Aa` is `m`-pseudo-coherent relative to `R` as a module over itself.

Both localizations are abstract — only `IsLocalization.Away` is assumed — so the statement applies
directly to the sections of a scheme on a standard open, which are a localization but not the
localization `Localization.Away`.

Two special cases are what a locality argument on a morphism of schemes consumes. With `s := 1`,
so that `Rs = R`, it localizes the *source* with the base fixed: shrinking the affine open of the
source to a standard open of itself. In general it does both at once: growing the affine open of
the target from a standard open `V'` back to `V` while shrinking the source.

Tag 0679 is stated for an arbitrary object of `D(A)` and its derived extension of scalars; here
the object is `A` in degree zero, whose derived extension of scalars is `Aa` in degree zero
because localization is flat. That identification is
`PseudoCoherence.derivedExtensionScalarsSingleIsoOfFlat`, whose hypothesis that `Aa` be
pseudo-coherent relative to `A` is
`PseudoCoherence.isModuleRelativelyPseudoCoherent_localizationAway_base`, and the contraction
`Aa ⊗_A A ≅ Aa` is `Algebra.TensorProduct.rid`. -/
public theorem moduleRelativelyPseudoCoherentFrom_localizationAway
    {R : Type u} {Rs : Type u} {A : Type u} {Aa : Type u}
    [CommRing R] [CommRing Rs] [CommRing A] [CommRing Aa]
    [Algebra R Rs] (s : R) [IsLocalization.Away s Rs]
    [Algebra Rs A] [Algebra.FiniteType Rs A] [Algebra R A] [IsScalarTower R Rs A]
    (a : A) [Algebra A Aa] [IsLocalization.Away a Aa]
    [Algebra R Aa] [IsScalarTower R A Aa] (m : ℤ)
    (h : IsModuleRelativelyPseudoCoherentFrom (R := Rs) (A := A) A m) :
    letI : Algebra.FiniteType R Rs :=
      IsLocalization.finiteType_of_monoid_fg (Submonoid.powers s) Rs
    letI : Algebra.FiniteType R A := Algebra.FiniteType.trans
      (inferInstance : Algebra.FiniteType R Rs) (inferInstance : Algebra.FiniteType Rs A)
    letI : Algebra.FiniteType A Aa :=
      IsLocalization.finiteType_of_monoid_fg (Submonoid.powers a) Aa
    letI : Algebra.FiniteType R Aa := Algebra.FiniteType.trans
      (inferInstance : Algebra.FiniteType R A) (inferInstance : Algebra.FiniteType A Aa)
    IsModuleRelativelyPseudoCoherentFrom (R := R) (A := Aa) Aa m := by
  let : Algebra.FiniteType R Rs :=
    IsLocalization.finiteType_of_monoid_fg (Submonoid.powers s) Rs
  let : Algebra.FiniteType R A := Algebra.FiniteType.trans
    (inferInstance : Algebra.FiniteType R Rs) (inferInstance : Algebra.FiniteType Rs A)
  let : Algebra.FiniteType A Aa :=
    IsLocalization.finiteType_of_monoid_fg (Submonoid.powers a) Aa
  let : Algebra.FiniteType R Aa := Algebra.FiniteType.trans
    (inferInstance : Algebra.FiniteType R A) (inferInstance : Algebra.FiniteType A Aa)
  have : Module.Flat A Aa := IsLocalization.flat Aa (Submonoid.powers a)
  have hAa : IsModuleRelativelyPseudoCoherent (R := A) (A := Aa) Aa :=
    isModuleRelativelyPseudoCoherent_localizationAway_base a
  have h0679 := (localization_preserves_relativePseudoCoherent
    (R := R) (Rf := Rs) (A := A) (Ag := Aa) s a
    ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of A A)) m).1 h
  refine relativelyPseudoCoherentFrom_of_iso (R := R) ?_ h0679
  exact derivedExtensionScalarsSingleIsoOfFlat hAa A ≪≫
    (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} Aa) 0).mapIso
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.rid A Aa Aa).toLinearEquiv.toModuleIso

/-- **Relative pseudo-coherence of a module does not see a principal localization of the base.**
The module form of `PseudoCoherence.relativelyPseudoCoherent_iff_baseLocalizationAway`. -/
public theorem moduleRelativelyPseudoCoherent_iff_baseLocalizationAway
    {R : Type u} {Rs : Type u} {B : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing Rs] [CommRing B]
    [Algebra R Rs] (s : R) [IsLocalization.Away s Rs]
    [Algebra Rs B] [Algebra R B] [IsScalarTower R Rs B] [Algebra.FiniteType Rs B]
    (M : Type u) [AddCommGroup M] [Module B M] (m : ℤ) :
    letI : Algebra.FiniteType R Rs :=
      IsLocalization.finiteType_of_monoid_fg (Submonoid.powers s) Rs
    letI : Algebra.FiniteType R B :=
      Algebra.FiniteType.trans (R := R) (S := Rs) (A := B) inferInstance inferInstance
    (IsModuleRelativelyPseudoCoherentFrom (R := Rs) (A := B) M m ↔
      IsModuleRelativelyPseudoCoherentFrom (R := R) (A := B) M m) ∧
    (IsModuleRelativelyPseudoCoherent (R := Rs) (A := B) M ↔
      IsModuleRelativelyPseudoCoherent (R := R) (A := B) M) :=
  relativelyPseudoCoherent_iff_baseLocalizationAway s _ m

end PseudoCoherence

end
